        {
          "id": 2589005222,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "9a695d95 introduced a change in how FID names were generated.  They are now prefixed with a \", \" (comma + space), so \"File: myfile\" becomes \", File: myfile\".  The MS-WSP is looking for \"File: myfile\" as a FID name and since it doesn't exist (because of the added comma+space in the string), it doesn't dissect anything.  This patch removes the  comma + space in the FID name and I'm hoping that doesn't affect any SMB2 traffic.",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fad119898ba16a3f8be2f765dcff399098444abd4f85a04d4c3ef415a2bbe3d9?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mmann78"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-27T01:26:18.990Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-27T23:34:05.262Z",
