        {
          "id": 2591145245,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Your patch to the FID name should not negatively impact the proper dissection, filtering, or search of FID names in SMB2 captures because the change I made was merely cosmetic. The filename itself is unaffected by my change or yours; only the string appended to COL_INFO is. Does this mean that the MS-WSP dissector looks for the filename string in COL_INFO? That string is for users not dissectors.",
